WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:03.700
The growing ecosystem of IBM Cloud for Financial Services,

00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:06.640
a free way to learn Kubernetes with IBM CloudLabs,

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:09.620
and policy-based governance in a trusted container platform

00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:12.180
- all on this episode of IBM Cloud Now.

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:15.739
Hey everyone, I'm Ian, and I'm excited to
be back to bring you the latest and greatest

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:18.360
news and announcements from IBM Cloud.

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:20.900
Last year, in collaboration with Bank of America,

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:23.540
IBM designed an industry-first platform called

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:25.400
IBM Cloud for Financial Services

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:28.610
that leverages the highest levels of encryption certification.

00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:32.700
Essentially, it's the world's first financial
services-ready public cloud.

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:35.280
In addition to offering a secured cloud platform,

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:38.820
we believe it is equally important to build a trusted ecosystem around it.

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:42.499
That's why we're thrilled to announce that more than 30 partners have joined our ecosystem

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:44.340
in the past three months alone.

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:47.760
Together, we're working to create a secure financial services ecosystem

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:50.700
where banks, ISV partners, and SaaS providers

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:54.020
can define and monitor their security and compliance obligations

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:55.850
and transact with confidence.

00:00:55.850 --> 00:00:58.740
We also provide a wide variety of co-creation opportunities,

00:00:58.740 --> 00:00:59.880
selling networks,

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:02.749
and personalized go-to-market support for our partners.

00:01:02.749 --> 00:01:05.540
If you're interested in learning more about
the opportunities and how your company can

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:08.840
join the ecosystem, see the link in the description
below.

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:11.760
Next up, I want to talk about IBM CloudLabs,

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:13.880
a really cool new set of interactive Kubernetes

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:16.400
tutorials that are completely free to use.

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:18.780
IBM CloudLabs offers hands-on,

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:20.900
browser-based training for deploying and operating

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:24.640
one free cluster on the&nbsp; IBM Cloud Kubernetes Service for 3 hours.

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:26.640
No downloads or configuration required.

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:30.000
All the tools you need are embedded right in the terminal in the browser.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.120
In just 3 easy steps, you can earn a certification badge.

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:35.180
Just sign up for a free IBM Cloud account,

00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:36.640
complete the tutorial coursework

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:38.020
through 5 interactive labs,

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:40.560
and then put your knowledge to the test by taking a quiz.

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:41.380
And that's it!

00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:43.620
It's a fantastic way to get some hands-on
experience

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:45.860
with operating Kubernetes on IBM Cloud,

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:49.130
- and who doesn't like a good certification badge for their efforts?

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:52.280
To learn more about this free opportunity, click on the link I've got below.

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:54.200
Finally, to close out this episode,

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:57.340
I wanted to touch on a partnership between NIST, IBM,

00:01:57.340 --> 00:01:58.480
Red Hat, and Intel

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:01.640
to build a trusted container platform based on OpenShift.

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:04.760
The platform ensures that workloads are run on trustworthy nodes,

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:06.140
with integrity established

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:07.910
via hardware root of trust.

00:02:07.910 --> 00:02:10.520
It also protects workload confidentiality
and keys,

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:12.170
which is really important when dealing

00:02:12.170 --> 00:02:15.030
with regulated or sensitive applications and
data.

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:16.460
This is the first demonstration

00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:18.660
of a container platform with this level of assurance

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:21.000
and it's really interesting and innovative stuff.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.630
If you check out the linked article below,

00:02:22.630 --> 00:02:23.980
you can learn more about the building blocks

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:27.320
and architecture for this trusted container  platform.

00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:30.200
Thanks for joining me today for this episode
of IBM Cloud Now.

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:32.500
If you're interested in learning more about the topics I've covered,

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:35.090
make sure you explore the links in the description of this video.

00:02:35.090 --> 00:02:36.020
And, of course,

00:02:36.020 --> 00:02:38.640
please don't forget to subscribe to our channel to stay up-to-date

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:40.680
on what's going on in the cloud, now.

